&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;This is a re-mix of Smight&amp;#39;s lovely Vectored thrust VTOL (https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:4639577). I&amp;#39;ve added a peg hole to fit my hex flight stand (https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:4766450) as well as included a version of the engines with exhaust that won&amp;#39;t need the flight peg. With the exhaust version, you&amp;#39;ll need to print it twice with one copy mirrored and print the main body of the VTOL from the original design.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Please see the instructions at https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:4766450 for how I recommend printing the stand.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;I had great success printing the aircraft itself on my Ender 3 by angling it up 45 degrees, which greatly reduced layer lines and gave it a clean underside.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;If you like this, please consider a tip to Smight: https://www.thingiverse.com/smight/designs
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
